# System Requirements

## Project Objective

Design and prototype a compact automotive RF sensing system capable of detecting and characterizing radar emissions in a vehicle environment.

The system will use software-defined radio (SDR), signal processing, and custom hardware to identify candidate radar signals and provide an alert to the user.

## Primary Requirements

### RF Sensing

* Detect RF signals within the selected operating frequency range.
* Measure signal frequency and relative signal strength.
* Distinguish candidate radar signals from background RF noise.
* Operate in real time or near-real time.

### Signal Processing

* Acquire IQ data from an SDR.
* Generate frequency-domain representations using FFTs.
* Estimate the local noise floor.
* Detect signals exceeding defined thresholds.
* Extract measurable signal characteristics.
* Develop a basic signal classification method.

### User Interface

* Display detected signal information.
* Provide an audible or visual alert when a candidate signal is detected.
* Display system status and relevant measurements.

### Mechanical

* Design a compact enclosure using CAD.
* Provide secure mounting for the electronics.
* Consider vibration and temperature encountered in an automotive environment.
* Provide appropriate ventilation or thermal management if required.

### Electrical

* Operate from an automotive 12 V power source or suitable portable power supply.
* Protect electronics from inappropriate input voltage.
* Minimize system power consumption where practical.

## Performance Metrics

The prototype will be experimentally evaluated using:

* Detection sensitivity
* Detection range
* False-positive rate
* Detection latency
* Frequency estimation accuracy
* Signal-to-noise ratio
* Power consumption
* Operating temperature

## Project Constraints

* Semester-scale development timeline
* Student/research prototype rather than commercial product
* Reasonable component cost
* Testing conducted in compliance with applicable laws and regulations

## Stretch Goals

The following features will only be attempted after the core system is functional:

* Direction-of-arrival estimation
* Multiple-antenna sensing
* Improved signal classification
* Custom PCB
* Custom automotive enclosure
* Environmental/vibration testing
* On-device processing without a laptop
